  "construction": "Pair-partition CPM CSS code (the pair-partition rule and girth rule of Okada-Kasai, arXiv:2607.14091) on a sparse 6x14 template of check weight 6, cyclic lift P = 21 (Z_21), n = 14P = 294, k = 2P = 42, design rate 1/7. Template: 6 block rows per type on 14 block columns, every block row of weight 6, every block column of degree 2 or 3 on each side (8 of degree 3, 6 of degree 2; the degree-2 columns of a side form a connected unicyclic graph on its rows). Block columns per block row: X = [[0,1,2,4,5,12], [0,2,3,5,7,13], [1,2,4,8,9,10], [3,4,6,7,9,10], [5,6,7,11,12,13], [8,9,10,11,12,13]], Z = [[0,1,2,3,5,6], [0,2,3,7,8,11], [0,3,4,7,9,13], [1,4,5,6,12,13], [4,6,8,9,10,12], [5,7,8,10,11,12]]. Qubit u*P + s is position s in Z_21 of block column u; X-check (i,r), r in Z_21, acts on the qubits u*P + ((r + e_iu) mod P), u in X_i, Z-check (j,r) on u*P + ((r + f_ju) mod P), u in Z_j; checks in the order i*P + r. Exponents (u:e per block row): X0: 0:0 1:0 2:0 4:0 5:0 12:0; X1: 0:0 2:20 3:0 5:14 7:0 13:0; X2: 1:0 2:14 4:19 8:14 9:19 10:0; X3: 3:10 4:0 6:16 7:11 9:20 10:12; X4: 5:0 6:7 7:9 11:8 12:2 13:19; X5: 8:1 9:5 10:1 11:1 12:0 13:5; Z0: 0:0 1:0 2:14 3:15 5:14 6:0; Z1: 0:0 2:0 3:0 7:1 8:0 11:0; Z2: 0:0 3:11 4:0 7:11 9:0 13:0; Z3: 1:0 4:19 5:19 6:14 12:0 13:5; Z4: 4:0 6:5 8:16 9:20 10:1 12:0; Z5: 5:0 7:7 8:1 10:8 11:8 12:0. Every overlap of an X-row and a Z-row of the template has 0, 2 or 4 block columns and splits into pairs {u,v} with e_iu - f_ju = e_iv - f_jv, so H_X H_Z^T = 0; the pairing satisfies the girth rule (no pair in two cells of one row or one column of the pairing array), and no two checks of one type share two qubits. rank H_X = rank H_Z = 6P = 126; every check has weight 6; qubit (X, Z)-degrees (2,2) on 42, (2,3) on 84, (3,2) on 84 and (3,3) on 84 qubits. The pairing square complex (template rows and columns, one square per pair) has first Betti number 3 and torsion-free H_1; the exponents are a class of H^1 with values in Z_21.",
